    "task": null,
    "text": "Finding from `private/archive-operations.md` (researcher): archive member names can contain Windows backslashes although extraction runs on Linux. POSIX-only path validation may miss `..` traversal and drive/UNC absolute forms before extraction (e.g. `assets\\\\..\\\\outside.txt`, `C:\\\\temp\\\\outside.txt`, `\\\\\\\\server\\\\share\\\\outside.txt`). Normalize `\\\\` to `/` before path checks; reject names that become absolute or contain a `..` component, while allowing safe nested relative paths.",
    "view": {
      "at_ms": 1791134886085,
      "author": "5c3079edb04e21b8ab686047b53f19f3aa9a8fb5347ce814e257e4e6494f596a",
